<%--
_Sys_Time_Until - a moment in the future, counted down in words: "33 minutes from now".

$time (required) - the moment, as an ISO datetime string.

The text is rewritten every second for as long as the component is on the page, so it
needs no refresh from its host. Once the moment has passed it reads "any moment now": the
thing it names (a task's estimated completion) is late, not finished. The exact time is the
element's title.

    <_Sys_Time_Until $time=task.eta_at />
--%>
<Define:_Sys_Time_Until tag="span">
    <% if (!this.args.time) { throw new Error('_Sys_Time_Until requires $time'); } %>
    <span $sid="text" title="<%= Rsx_Time.format_timestamp(this.args.time) %>"><%= _Sys_Time_Until.phrase(Rsx_Time.seconds_until(this.args.time)) %></span>
</Define:_Sys_Time_Until>
